## Original Content
The primary runoff in South Carolina between Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman is another test of President Trump's influence. He's backing Darline, sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham.

## Summary
The primary runoff election in South Carolina for the U.S. Senate is a test of President Trump's political influence, with Trump endorsing Sen. Darline Graham. Darline Graham is the sister of the late Sen. Lindsey Graham. This election could indicate the effectiveness of Trump's endorsements in shaping political outcomes.

## Key Points
- The U.S. Senate runoff in South Carolina features Sen. Darline Graham and Rep. Ralph Norman.
- The election is viewed as a key test of President Trump's influence in politics.
- President Trump has publicly endorsed Darline Graham in this race.
- Darline Graham is related to the late Sen. Lindsey Graham, adding a familial connection to the political context.


